# frontend/.prettierignore (rename to .prettierignore) — gitignore syntax, paths relative to
# frontend/. Keep it SHORT: prettier already skips node_modules by default, and by default it
# reads BOTH .gitignore and .prettierignore — so `dist/`, `dist-ssr/` and `*.local` are already
# covered by frontend/.gitignore and must NOT be repeated here.
#
# THE TRAP: passing `--ignore-path` (any value) REPLACES that default pair instead of adding to
# it. `prettier --check . --ignore-path .prettierignore` stops reading .gitignore, walks into
# frontend/dist, and reports the minified bundle you just built as badly formatted. Run plain
# `prettier --check .` / `prettier --write .` and let the defaults do their job.
#
# This file is for the leftovers .gitignore has no opinion about: generated or vendored files
# that ARE committed, and files whose exact bytes matter to something other than a human.

# Generated from the backend's OpenAPI schema, if you add that step — prettier reformatting a
# generated file makes every regeneration a diff.
# src/api-types.generated.ts

# Vendored third-party source committed into the repo, if any.
# src/vendor/

# Snapshot / fixture files whose exact bytes are the test.
# src/**/__snapshots__/
